you pick between asuka, rei and shinji, each character has their stats and abilities

there is a stage for each angel, 
the fights are like undertale, 
each win, depending on your score
you get level points, level points let you upgrade character stats and 
unlock new agilities

battle mechanics:

sync rate: the higher your sync rate, the more accurate your hits, the more powerful
your attacks

at field: defense, id upgraded with level points

to boost sync rate: player heart beats and evangelion heart beats,
player has to press when eva heart beats, the more correct presses, the higher
sync rate

attack stack: minecraft fishing mechanic, it gets harder, but every correct one
adds another blow

evangelion knife attack: friday night funking
gun: undertale power bar

enemies have weak zones, they are harder to hit but deal more damage, taking them
out kill the enemy, you can also destroy the other enemies body parts, it's easier
but then you need to destroy every body part to kill the enemy

reaction time: the evangelion scans for openings, then once it appears
it says strike and the user has to press a, the faster the more damage

berserk mode: sync rate must be 100: user powers up the attack with hone + fishing,
super mega big attack but it sets sync rate to 3 and takes away health

enemy attacks:

bullet hell
laser beams on the screen
attacks fall: like that car game with lanes and you have to move the car to dodge
traffic
multiple weaping angel enemies like boos from mario
minefield: there are explosive markers around the floor that keep spawning and
player has to avoid them
angel grabs eva: press buttons as they appear on screen to escape otherwise
lost health

you get level points depending on how well you played, like ultrakill

character specific abilities:

Asuka: when at low sync rate (bellow  10%): focus ability: do hone attack but it
deals much much more damage

Shinji: divine gift, when low on health, kaworu comes and makes player invincible
for one round but only happens once per game

Rei: spear of longinus: if gets a good score at least 3 consecutive times, summonds
spear of longinus and deals a lot of damage: 100% accuracy

more abilities:

ruthless: when enemy is low on HP, attacks deal more damage
counter: if you don't take damage from previous attack, you deal x more damage
calm: instead of attacking, minigame to regain health
absolute accuracy: next attack doesn't miss
overclock: attack does x% more damage but your at field goes to 0 and you lose
x hp
double or nothing: your attack either does double damage or misses, chance varies
based on sync rate at 100% sync rate, chance of hitting is 70% and at 0 it's 10%
eek! run! : skip attack but enemy attack is easier to evade

player can purchase abilities with level points, the character specific
abilites are just free for the specific character and can be bought for other
characters

game modes:

easy: enemies deal less damage, easier to attack -> gives very very little level points
vanilla: vanilla -> normal amount of level points
hard: enemies deal more damage, harder to attack -> a bit more level points
helpless: you can't attack, you can only dodge until enemy's stamina runs out
marathon: defeat all of the bosses one by one without dying and without
refilling health -> unlocks any ability

player can pick 1 ability and unlock more slots with level points

practice mode -> combat lab

once you beat the game you unlock more challenges:

harder variants of the angels


endless mode: like marathon mode but you regain health and the longer you survive
the higher your score goes, no rewards just a high score thing, the premise is
the evangelion training room

pilot mastery: complete quests to unlock pilot cosmetics and character
exclusive abilities

randomized battle: random angel, random pilot, random abilites, modifier
modifier: enemy has more health, enemy has more attakc, or whatever

max ability 4 slots

has to beat the previous angel before unlocking the next angel

